{
 "id": "T09",
 "title": "Hypertension registry: component vs composite blood-pressure search",
 "scenario": "A hypertension registry flags patients whose blood pressure is above goal (systolic >= 140 or diastolic >= 90 mmHg). Blood pressure arrives as LOINC 85354-9 panels with systolic and diastolic components; one device sent a diastolic component with a dataAbsentReason, one device reports decimals, one interface sends a standalone systolic Observation, and a heart-rate Observation sits alongside. You are checking which resources each query the registry issues will return.",
 "server_timezone": "America/New_York",
 "why_hard": "component-code and component-value-quantity are separate parameters, so combining them with & matches when the code is on one component and the value on another (FHIR R4 search: parameters are evaluated independently; composite parameters exist to join them). component-code-value-quantity binds code and value to the SAME component. Two composite parameters joined by & may be satisfied by different components. value-quantity looks at Observation.value only, never components; the composite parameters look at components only (or Observation.code+value for code-value-quantity). eq on '140' is the range [139.5, 140.5).",
